      en: "Sunnyside Garden is a 0.5-hectare (1.2-acre) private botanical garden in the parish of St. George, established in 1980 by the Grant family. The garden features over 300 plant species, including many endemic to Grenada such as the Grenada orchid (Oncidium guttatum). It operates as a sustainable farm, producing spices like nutmeg, cinnamon, and turmeric. The garden also grows fruits like soursop and passionfruit. Guided tours educate visitors on permaculture and traditional uses of plants. The garden includes a small pond with koi and a shaded gazebo. Admission is $5, by appointment only. The property is at an elevation of 100 meters.",
